   "evidence": "Tensor.lean:58-62 states the claim unqualified; the analogous unpolarized discussion at Tensors/Basic.lean:725-729 explicitly records that \"exhaustion is false for an arbitrary abstract V and g: if the stabilizer of the kinematics is trivial then IsLorentzCovariant is vacuous and any conserved symmetric W qualifies\", and bundles the needed inputs in `SpectatorAssumptions` (Tensors/Basic.lean:736). Conservation in both slots for `\u03b5.bilinMap ![q, a]` holds for every `a` by `AlternatingMap.bilinMap_apply_left_eq_zero`/`_right_eq_zero` (Alternating/BilinMap.lean:75,81), which is what makes the `\u03c6` counterexample go through.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/Polarized/Tensor.lean",
   "fix": "Add the missing hypothesis to the sentence, e.g. \"the alternating forms that are conserved in both slots, linear in `S`, and invariant under the isometries fixing `p` and `q` (`Tensors.Hadronic.IsLorentzCovariant`)\", as the symmetric counterpart's exhaustion discussion does.",
   "issue": "The \"Not included\" section claims that on a 4-dimensional `V` (with `p`, `q`, `S` independent, `Q\u00b2 \u2260 0`, `S\u00b7q \u2260 0`) \"the alternating forms that are conserved in both slots *and linear in `S`* form a two-dimensional space spanned by `E\u2081` and `E\u2082`\". Without a covariance restriction this is false: for any linear `\u03c6 : V \u2192 V`, `S \u21a6 \u03b5(\u00b7, \u00b7, q, \u03c6 S)` is alternating, conserved in both slots and linear in `S`, so that space has dimension dim(V)\u00b7dim(V/\u27e8q\u27e9) = 12, not 2. The count is 2 only for forms built from `p`, `q`, `S` alone.",
   "line": 58
  }
 ],
